  "holistic_F_N": 2,
  "holistic_F_H": -1,
  "section_notes": "S1 is weakened because it covers only serious incidents, leaving minor overheating/smoke unreportable. S2 keeps the 5% benchmark but makes it a corrective-action trigger rather than a sales stop, allows open-ended continued sale, and requires per-model rates to customers but not public publication. S3 requires new-unit shut-off by 24 months and retrofit within 72 months only where technically feasible, with no alternative measure. S4 requires built-in suppression at 36 months, and S5 mandates recall at 8 per 100k with 5-business-day safety notices but no serious-injury clause."
